================================== P4  Mason-Stothers polynomial  X^p + Y^p = Z^p   (m=n=r=p) ==================================
A=X^p, B=Y^p, C=Z^p in Q[X,Y,Z]: pairwise coprime, max degree = p.
Claim to verify numerically (specialised):
  det [[A',B',C'],[1,1,1],[A",B",C"]] = const * prod cyclic (X-Y) * (sum of monomial symmetric form)
and  deg(rad((A-B)(B-C)(C-A))) = 3p > p,  matching Mason-Stothers'
prediction  max(degA,degB,degC) < deg(rad(...))  for this symmetric specialisation.
p=3:
   claim A' = p X^(p-1), ...  det = const * (X^(?) -)  coefficients below
   det (factored):
      -18*(X - Y)*(X - Z)*(Y - Z)
   rad((A-B)(B-C)(C-A)) (factored):  (X - Y)*(X - Z)*(Y - Z)*(X**2 + X*Y + Y**2)*(X**2 + X*Z + Z**2)*(Y**2 + Y*Z + Z**2)
